// origin/main: this five-line program NEVER TERMINATES under -O.
//
//   $ madaros --native-v2-compile repro_main_hangs_on_array_fill.sio -O -o x.elf
//   $ ./x.elf          # hangs; rc=124 under `timeout`
//
// Change [7; 4] to [0; 4] and it terminates -- because a zero fill skips the
// fill loop entirely in lower_array_repeat_literal_ref. So the non-termination
// is IN THE FILL LOOP.
//
// TWO DEFECTS ARE STACKED HERE, and they are separable:
//
//   #1682  ocp_mfi_dce_once marks a register used only from src1/src2, and
//          IrIndexSet keeps its third operand (the value) in imm_i64. The fill
//          value is therefore invisible and its load_imm is deleted. Same code,
//          byte for byte, on main and on this branch. -> wrong array contents.
//
//   #1667  the four propagation peels carry a table across block boundaries
//          with no invalidation at labels or terminators, which makes loops
//          under -O hang. Confirmed still live on main by the standalone
//          loop shape in tests/run-pass/opt_block_boundary_propagation.sio:
//          origin/main rc=124, this branch prints 70.
//
// #1682 alone gives a WRONG ANSWER. #1667 is what turns it into a HANG. That is
// why this branch prints 7 while main spins: the branch fixed #1667 first, which
// converted the hang into the wrong value that then exposed #1682.
//
// Refs #1682, #1667, #1649

fn main() -> i64 with IO, Mut, Panic, Div {
    var a: [i64; 4] = [7; 4]
    print_int(a[0 as usize])
    print("\n")
    0
}
